    "title": "Big Rock Teenage Angler says record catch enhances his love for fishing - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jay Hardy ,\n6 hours ago\nKENLY, N.C. (WNCT) — An exclusive interview with Nine on Your Side’s Jay Hardy as he catches up with Connor Daniel, the teenage fisherman, who brought in the incredible catch at last month’s Big Rock Blue Marlin Tournament in Morehead City, N.C.\n“He came all the way out of the water, ate the bait, and we knew…right then, it was over…” said Connor Daniel, Marlin Fever Angler.\nDay Two of the 2026 Big Rock…and the fight had just begun…18-year-old Daniel of Marlin Fever taking on what would be a record-setting blue marlin.\nDaniel said the fight lasted for two and a half hours…a time he will never forget.\nClick the video above for more.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WNCT.",
    "summary": "KENLY, N.C. (WNCT) — An exclusive interview with Nine on Your Side’s Jay Hardy as he catches up with Connor Daniel, the teenage fisherman, who brought in the incredible catch at last month’s Big Rock Blue Marlin Tournament in Morehead City, N.C. “He came all the way out of the water, ate the bait, and we knew…right then, it was over…” said Connor Daniel, Marlin Fever Angler. Daniel said the fight lasted for two and a half hours…a time he will never forget. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
